{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2518","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2518","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2518\",\"parent_revision\":\"bb2443065fd8f3147e2459dbdbe4478b611215c9590a496d9a640602aa41e91d\",\"root_revision\":\"bb2443065fd8f3147e2459dbdbe4478b611215c9590a496d9a640602aa41e91d\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-06-04\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nWhen `backlog_view(include_content=True)` is called with a non-exact section filter (substring, regex `/pattern/`, or numeric index), `_build_sections_metadata` still performs exact case-insensitive header matching. As a result:\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-06-04)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n- Goal: Fix `result.sections` desync with `result.body` when non-exact section filters (numeric index, comma-separated indices, regex, non-exact substring) are passed to `backlog_view`\\\\n- Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\\\n- AVAILABLE:\\\\n  - Root cause precisely identified: `_build_sections_metadata` uses exact case-insensitive name match (`sec_name.lower() != section_name_filter.lower()`) while `_apply_body_section_filter` uses four-form dispatch via `_resolve_section_indices`\\\\n  - Failing behavior reproducible via existing RED tests in `test_view_sections_metadata_sync.py` class `TestSectionsMetadataInSync`\\\\n  - Two fix options enumerated in the issue with clear trade-offs\\\\n  - View assembly pipeline call sites identified (lines 3199-3219 and 3231-3232 in `operations.py`)\\\\n  - Commit `dd334fb` confirmed as the origin of the independent matching paths\\\\n- DERIVABLE:\\\\n  - Fix scope derivable from Option 2: call `_build_sections_metadata(body, show, since, section=None)` after `_apply_body_section_filter` narrows the body so all headers in the narrowed body are captured\\\\n  - Pagination path (line 3253) derivably already consistent with Option 2\\\\n- MISSING:\\\\n  - Test run result to confirm RED vs GREEN status of `TestSectionsMetadataInSync` before implementation (establishes baseline)\\n\\n### Artifact Classification\\n\\n- Primary artifact type: Bug fix\\n- Behavioral boundary: `backlog_view` MCP tool call \u2014 `result.sections` dict when `section=` filter is used\\n- Domain-semantic evaluation target: For any valid resolved section filter form (numeric, comma, regex, substring), `result.sections` must contain exactly the metadata keys for headers present in `result.body`. The two fields must stay in sync.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Call `backlog_view(selector=\\\"<item with multiple sections>\\\", summary=False, include_content=True, section=\\\"2\\\")` (numeric form)\\n2. Observe `result.body` is narrowed to the third section (index 2)\\n3. Observe `result.sections == {}` despite body containing a valid section\\n4. Repeat with `section=\\\"/Impact.*/\\\"` (regex): body shows Impact section, sections is `{}`\\n5. Repeat with `section=\\\"Issue\\\"` (non-exact substring matching two headers): body shows both, sections is `{}`\\n6. Contrast: `section=\\\"RT-ICA\\\"` (exact name) correctly populates `result.sections`\\n\\nRoot cause: `_build_sections_metadata` at line 2725 uses `sec_name.lower() != section_name_filter.lower()` (exact match only). When called from the view pipeline after body narrowing, if `section` is passed as a non-exact form, the exact-match guard skips all headers. Fix: call with `section=None` after narrowing so all headers in the narrowed body are captured.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- `result.sections == {}` for numeric, regex, and non-exact-substring filter forms\\n- `result.body` correctly narrowed in all three forms\\n- RED tests: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_view_sections_metadata_sync.py`, class `TestSectionsMetadataInSync`\\n- Commit `dd334fb` introduced `_resolve_section_indices` and `_slice_body_by_header_indices`; `_build_sections_metadata` was not updated to share that dispatch\\n- PR #2501 review comments: `PRRT_kwDOQGimCs6F4f1j` and `PRRT_kwDOQGimCs6F4f35`\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Body path works correctly; section metadata is silently dropped for three of four advertised filter forms. High priority: agents using progressive disclosure or section-count checks on numeric/regex filter results receive silent empty metadata.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Agents and clients using `result.sections` for routing with numeric or regex filter forms\\n- Three of four advertised filter forms are broken for the sections map\\n- Silent failure: callers receive `{}` sections with no error signal\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- All four filter forms behave consistently: body and sections dict always in sync\\n- Progressive disclosure patterns using numeric section indices correctly populate metadata\\n- Eliminates a class of silent data loss in the backlog_view contract\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `backlog_view` is called with any valid section filter form, `result.sections` contains exactly the metadata for headers present in the narrowed `result.body`. `set(result.sections.keys()) == set(header names in result.body)` for any resolved filter. A genuine miss yields `body==\\\"\\\"`, `sections=={}`, `section_filter_miss==True`.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nAfter `_apply_body_section_filter` narrows the body, `_build_sections_metadata` must be called on the narrowed body with `section=None` (not with the original filter string). This captures all headers in the already-narrowed body. The fix applies to the non-paginated path (line 3219) and must be consistent with the paginated path (line 3253). Option 2 from the issue is the lower-risk fix: no signature changes to `_build_sections_metadata`.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Numeric form: `backlog_view(section=\\\"2\\\")` \u2014 `result.sections` contains the header-2 metadata key; `set(result.sections.keys()) == set(header names in result.body)`\\n2. Regex form: `backlog_view(section=\\\"/Impact.*/\\\")` \u2014 `result.sections == {\\\"Impact Radius\\\": ...}`; body and sections in sync\\n3. Substring form: `backlog_view(section=\\\"Issue\\\")` matching two headers \u2014 `result.sections` contains both matched headers' metadata\\n4. Exact-name regression guard: `backlog_view(section=\\\"RT-ICA\\\")` still correctly populates `result.sections == {\\\"RT-ICA\\\": ...}`\\n5. Genuine miss (`section=\\\"/zzz-nomatch/\\\"`) produces `result.sections == {}`, `result.body == \\\"\\\"`, `section_filter_miss == True`\\n6. All tests in `TestSectionsMetadataInSync` in `test_view_sections_metadata_sync.py` pass GREEN\\n7. Paginated path (`offset`/`limit` with non-exact section filter) also produces non-empty `result.sections` when the filter resolves\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 `_build_sections_metadata` (line 2688), `_resolve_section_indices` (line 2509), `_apply_body_section_filter` (line 3018), view assembly (line 3193) |\\n| Test | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_view_sections_metadata_sync.py` \u2014 `TestSectionsMetadataInSync` (RED tests for this defect) |\\n| Test | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_apply_body_section_filter_forms.py` |\\n| Test | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_view_section_filter.py` |\\n| Backlog | #2495 \u2014 parent defect introducing four-form dispatch |\\n| PR | #2501 \u2014 review comments flagging this gap |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: #2495 (four-form dispatch via `_resolve_section_indices` must be in place \u2014 confirmed present via commit `dd334fb`)\\n- Blocks: None identified\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Run `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/test_view_sections_metadata_sync.py -v -k 'numeric_section or regex_section or substring_section'` to confirm RED vs GREEN baseline before implementing\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 Targeted change in `operations.py` view assembly pipeline. Acceptance tests already written. Both fix options are well-scoped. Primary risk is ensuring miss-guard and pagination paths are not regressed.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nWhen `backlog_view(include_content=True)` is called with a non-exact section filter (substring, regex `/pattern/`, or numeric index), `_build_sections_metadata` still performs exact case-insensitive header matching. As a result:\\n\\n- `body` is correctly narrowed to the matched section\\n- `result.sections` is `{}` \u2014 empty, despite the matched section being present\\n\\nThis means clients consuming the `sections` map lose metadata for the matched section even though the body correctly reflects it.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root Cause\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`_build_sections_metadata` and `_resolve_section_indices` (the four-form dispatch introduced in `dd334fb`) use independent matching paths. The view assembly pipeline calls `_build_sections_metadata` first (exact match \u2192 empty sections for non-exact queries), then `_apply_body_section_filter` (four-form dispatch \u2192 correct body). The sections map is never rebuilt after the body is narrowed.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fix Options\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. Share the four-form dispatch logic: pass `_resolve_section_indices` results into `_build_sections_metadata` instead of re-matching from scratch\\n2. Rebuild sections metadata from the narrowed body after `_apply_body_section_filter` runs\\n</div>\\n\\n## References\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- PR #2501 review comments: `PRRT_kwDOQGimCs6F4f1j` (chatgpt-codex-connector P2) and `PRRT_kwDOQGimCs6F4f35` (copilot-pull-request-reviewer)\\n- Implementation introduced in commit `dd334fb` (`_resolve_section_indices`, `_slice_body_by_header_indices`)\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"1040eae15f99a8769b4be39949733c9df7512832299c932f06523c0b18ede8be\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCMVkA\"}"}